  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What the kernel adds",
      "items": [
        "mac80211 stack, absent in stock, enabled as CONFIG_MAC80211=y",
        "Atheros AR9271/AR7010, Ralink RT2800 and Realtek RTL8187/RTL8192CU as modules",
        "Verified capture: 802.11 radiotap, 907 frames in 15 s, 0 dropped by the kernel"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Why drivers are modules",
      "items": [
        "ath9k_htc and the vendor Qualcomm driver both use the HTC prefix",
        "Building =y fails at link time with duplicate symbol htc_stop",
        "Modules keep those symbols local to the .ko"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Traps worth knowing",
      "items": [
        "CROSS_COMPILE_COMPAT is required or the 32-bit VDSO links with the host linker",
        "firmware_class.path under /data returns EACCES: SELinux denies the kernel domain",
        "KernelSU-Next is incompatible with SUSFS patches after its tree restructure",
        "The only matching pair found: KernelSU susfs-legacy with susfs4ksu kernel-4.14"
      ]
    }
  ]
